Preventing Form Reloads with e.preventDefault()

When you submit an HTML form, the browser default behavior is to reload the entire page. In modern JavaScript apps, we stop that reload so our code can handle the submission smoothly:

```javascript
const form = document.querySelector("#signup-form");
form.addEventListener("submit", (event) => {
  event.preventDefault(); // Stop the page reload!
  console.log("Form processed with JavaScript!");
});
```
Remember: addEventListener("click", callback) listens for user actions; event.preventDefault() stops page reloads.

