The Golden Rule of Arrays: Zero-Indexed

Computers always start counting at zero! The first item is at index `0`, the second is at index `1`, and so on.

To iterate (loop) through every item, use `.forEach()`:

```javascript
languages.forEach((lang) => {
  console.log("I am learning: " + lang);
});
```
Remember: Arrays hold lists in square brackets [ ]; counting always begins at index 0.

