`localStorage` can ONLY store plain text strings. If you want to store a list of tasks or an object, you must convert it into a string using `JSON.stringify()` before saving:

```javascript
const tasks = ["Buy Milk", "Study CSS"];
localStorage.setItem("myTasks", JSON.stringify(tasks));

// When loading it back, convert string back to a real array:
const loadedTasks = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem("myTasks"));
```
Remember: Use JSON.stringify() to save arrays into localStorage, and JSON.parse() to load them back.

